I think there is a Codewars kata named "Abbreviate a Number" (6 kyu?) The expected function `abbrev_num(x)`. I might have seen solutions. They use:
def abbrev_num(x):
    if x < 1000: return str(x)
    for i, suffix in enumerate(['K','M','B','T']):
        if x < 1000**(i+2):
            num = x / 1000**(i+1)
            if num < 10:
                return f"{num:.1f}{suffix}"
            else:
                return f"{round(num)}{suffix}"
    return f"{x}?"
